course: dictionary
lesson: 9836
title: A swimmer and what makes one strong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A swimmer is a person or animal that swims. The ending -er often means someone who does something, like a runner, a singer or a swimmer. Look at the words around swimmer in a sentence to see who or what is swimming.
explain: «Tigers swim well and cool off in pools and rivers.» The clue is swim well, so a swimmer here is an animal that is good at swimming. Ask yourself: what word would fit in this place? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Being a strong swimmer does not make you safe in every water. «Cold water can make the body gasp and muscles stop working, even in strong swimmers.» Good swimmers still need care, so always swim where a lifeguard is on duty.
fact: A swimmer is a person or animal that swims, or who is swimming.
fact: A strong swimmer can swim well, and a weak swimmer cannot.
fact: Tigers, jaguars and fishing cats are happy swimmers, even though most cats dislike water.
fact: In water safety, swim between the red and yellow flags at a lifeguarded beach, and never swim alone.
fact: In Australia, informal use, swimmers means swimming costumes.
exercise: «Tigers swim well and cool off in pools and rivers.» In this sentence, what is a swimmer? | A low wall across a river | A fast runner on dry land | A fish that never leaves the sea | *A person or animal that swims
exercise: What is the difference between a strong swimmer and a weak swimmer? | A strong swimmer is always taller than a weak swimmer | They mean exactly the same thing | A weak swimmer is a person who swims in a race | *A strong swimmer can swim well, and a weak swimmer cannot
exercise: «Cold water can make the body gasp and muscles stop working, even in strong swimmers.» What does this sentence teach us? | Cold water makes every swimmer faster | Strong swimmers never need a lifeguard | Muscles work best in cold water | *Even strong swimmers can be in danger in cold water
test: Which swimming phrase means someone who swims in races against others? | Swimmers' ear | Weak swimmer | *Competitive swimmer | Strong swimmer
test: In water safety, what should you do if a swimmer is in trouble? | Wait until they swim back by themselves | Swim out alone to rescue them | *Call for help and throw something that floats | Jump in straight away without thinking
exam: «A weir is a low wall across a river... below it the water churns round and round and can hold a swimmer under, so never swim near a weir.» Why must you never swim near a weir? | Because the water below can churn and hold a swimmer under | Because boats always crash into the wall | Because weirs are made of soft sand | *Because weirs are too short to see from the bank
